@copilot Update PR #21401 directly on its verified branch `copilot/batch-2-migrate-standalone-tests` in `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation`. Keep the branch GitHub Copilot cloud agent assigned. Do not rename it, replace it, or create a separate PR. If GitHub itself assigns a follow-up branch, keep it.

Fix the coverage regression raised in Copilot review 6007260519. In `instrumentation/rediscala-1.8/javaagent/build.gradle.kts`, the existing `if (otelProps.denyUnsafe)` block disables every `Test` task. The migrated `unitTests` task inherits that block, so `RediscalaAttributesGetterTest`, `RediscalaServerTargetsTest`, and `ServerEndpointTest` no longer run under `-PdenyUnsafe=true`; the old standalone project did not have that skip. Scope the skip to the installed-agent `test` execution, using the repository's suite execution conventions. Keep the current installed-agent skip, continue scheduling `unitTests` under `check`, and preserve the existing Rediscala dependency pin and latest-dependency behavior. Limit the change to the relevant Gradle wiring; no production changes or new suites.

Apply the narrow Spotless task first, then verify where feasible that the Rediscala `unitTests` task executes with `-PdenyUnsafe=true` while the installed-agent `test` task remains skipped. Report any limitations. Do not reply to or resolve review threads; the coordinator will verify the fix and handle the thread.
